{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Crucible</b> — if. The husks of crushed wheat, and likewise the meaning is: a crucible serves silver to refine it." "<b>And furnace for gold</b> — to refine it." "<b>And a man</b> — that is, each person is refined and tested according to his praisers, meaning according to what was intended in praising him. But if you crush the fool in a mortar with force, his folly will not depart from him, as the husk of the chaff departs." "<b>And a man</b> — like 'and not a man was missing' (Numbers 31:49); it is not בֶּן־אָדָם."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:04.804159909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}